// ── THE IMAGE THIS FLEET BUILT ITSELF ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// The sweep above measured images someone else published. This one was built on spark-a3ee from
// vllm-project/vllm 07b75534651a0dd584c6f3be75d8c62fb8426397 by the modeled build in
// gunbc.spark.vllm_runtime_image_build, and probed inside its own digest by the executable probe in
// gunbc.spark.v41_runtime_image_probe -- the discharge the build obligation below asks for, taken on
// the same accelerator with the same questions.
//
// THE REFERENCE IS AN IMAGE ID AND NOT A REPOSITORY PATH, because this image was never pushed
// anywhere: it exists in one daemon's local store, and what identifies it there is the config digest
// that daemon reported. Spelling the derived build tag here instead would have made the subject of a
// receipt move whenever the recipe changed, which is the defect the readings above already corrected
// once -- an observation's subject is whatever was observed, permanently.
//
// ITS ARCHITECTURE ROW DERIVES FROM A READING LIKE EVERY ROW ABOVE. The full list the registry
// answered for is in gunbc.spark.runtime_architecture_registry_reading with its host, date and
// instrument, so this row asks that reading rather than carrying a second hand-written answer about
// the same run -- and the subject of both is the digest, not the derived build tag.
data v41_gb10_source_build_probe: ProbedRuntimeImage = ProbedRuntimeImage {
  image_reference: gunbc_vllm_dsv41_gb10_registry_reading.image_reference,
  framework: "vllm" as NonEmptyStr,
  framework_version: "0.1.dev1+g07b755346" as NonEmptyStr,
}

